      "diff": "@@ -13,9 +13,12 @@ It is used for troubleshooting, analysis, development and education.\n \n == What’s New\n \n-// This is the final release of the Wireshark 3.0 branch.\n-// It will reach its official end of life on Smarch 230, 2020.\n-// If you are still using Wireshark 3.0 you are encouraged to upgrade to Wireshark 3.4.\n+This is expected to be the final release of the Wireshark 3.0 branch.\n+It will reach its official end of life https://gitlab.com/wireshark/editor-wiki/-/wikis/Development/LifeCycle#end-of-life-planning[when Wireshark 3.4.0 is released].\n+If you are still using Wireshark 3.0 you are encouraged to upgrade to Wireshark 3.2 or 3.4.\n+\n+The Windows installers now ship with Qt 5.12.9.\n+They previously shipped with Qt 5.12.8.\n \n === Bug Fixes\n \n@@ -36,7 +39,20 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* wsbuglink:6000[Wireshark bug]\n //* cveidlink:2014-2486[]\n //* Wireshark slowly leaked water under the kitchen sink over the course of several months, causing a big mess.\n-// cp /dev/null /tmp/buglist.txt ; for bugnumber in `git log --stat v3.0.14rc0..| grep ' Bug:' | awk '{print $2}' | sort -n -u ` ; do \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/tools/gen-bugnote\" $bugnumber; pbpaste >> /tmp/buglist.txt; done\n+// cp /dev/null /tmp/buglist.txt ; for bugnumber in `git log --stat v3.0.14rc0.. | gsed -e 's/\\(close\\|fix\\|resolv\\)[^ ]* #/\\nclose #/gI' | grep ^close | sed -e 's/close.*#\\([1-9][0-9]*\\).*/\\1/' | sort -V -u` ; do \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/tools/gen-bugnote\" $bugnumber; pbpaste >> /tmp/buglist.txt; done\n+\n+* Buildbot crash output: randpkt-2019-04-01-28345.pcap wsbuglink:15661[].\n+\n+* Buildbot crash output: fuzz-2020-07-28-5905.pcap wsbuglink:16741[].\n+\n+* ERROR:epan/proto.c:9868:hfinfo_number_value_format_display: code should not be reached wsbuglink:16816[].\n+\n+* S1-U data forwarding info and S103 PDN data forwarding info IE's showing improper value wsbuglink:16777[].\n+\n+* The client timestamp is parsed error for Google QUIC (version Q039) wsbuglink:16839[].\n+\n+* Wireshark fails to detect libssh >= 0.9.5 wsbuglink:16845[].\n+\n \n === New and Updated Features\n \n@@ -59,6 +75,21 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n // Add one protocol per line between the -- delimiters.\n [commaize]\n --\n+AARP\n+BSSMAP\n+GQUIC\n+GSM A RR\n+GTPv2\n+MIME Multipart\n+NCP\n+NDS\n+PFCP\n+PROFINET\n+Q.933\n+TACACS+\n+TCP\n+S1AP\n+X2AP\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n",
